      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have this on some avatars when not using elbow trackers:\nElbows bend too much inwards:\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/946881839400882196/953200707874463764/20220315085625_1.jpg\nElbows break:\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/946881839400882196/953200486075490334/20220315085707_1.jpg\nAnother avatar where elbows break:\nhttps://media.discordapp.net/attachments/946881839400882196/953201861526188093/20220315090333_1.jpg?width=603&height=603\nI know for a fact my Mokuri has a very funky rig, though (time to attempt updating it to one of the fan-fixed bases, perhaps). Despite this, it has tended to work well in most applications I've thrown it into thus far. \nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/946881839400882196/953203896543752202/unknown.png\nAs far as I can tell my first avatars rigs seems to make sense in Blender at least.\nOne thing these two avatars have in common: A pose.\nAlthough I have had other A-posed avatars without much issue.\nOne thing these\nEDIT: I see now I should be posting screenshots of avatars in a world that visualizes the bones. I am not able to take more screenshots right now, so I will do this later as a reply to this post.",
